{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.DilogPartBFaddeevScaling","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DilogPartBFaddeevScaling","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.DilogPartBWP1Capstone","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.DilogPartBIteratedLimit"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.wp1_faddeev_tendsto","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.wp1_faddeev_tendsto","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogPartBFaddeevScaling.lean#L56-L110","doc":"**Faddeev-scaling W-P1 convergence (unconditional, cusp-reaching).**  For fixed\n`x ∈ (0,1)`, with the moving-target bulk index `n(q) = nOfQ x q (2−q)` (largest `n` with\n`x·qⁿ ≤ 2−q`), the positive-factor rescaled log-sum converges to the W-P1 target as\n`q → 1⁺`, with **no** Diophantine hypothesis:\n\n`(q − 1)·Σ_{k<n(q)} log(1 − x·qᵏ)  ⟶  Li₂(x) − π²/6`.\n\nProof: the endpoint `x·qⁿ ∈ ((2−q)/q, 2−q]` reaches the cusp (`→ 1⁻`, squeeze) while the\ngap `1 − x·qⁿ ≥ q − 1` gives the no-resonance bound with `c = 1`; then\n`tendsto_wp1_sum_of_no_resonance` (#4270) applies. ","signatureChunk":0}]}